// Two enumerators may not stand for the same number.  An enum is a set
// of things a program tells apart, and two names quietly sharing one
// number make '=' answer true for two of them with nothing in the text
// saying so.  Where it is meant, the second names the first.

enum E : u32:
    a = 1
    b = 1

@start
@impure
fn main():
    std.println("{}", E.a.ord())
